"""``kentos.cad``: KentOS CAD from Python (docs/adr/0131).

- :class:`Document`: a drawing without a window, the desktop's own
  document: ``Document.new(srid=5256)``, ``Document.open("ada.kcad")``.
- The commands, each under its catalog name and typed from the catalog's
  schemas: ``polygon.create(doc, layer_id=…, pts=[(x, y), …])``, with
  ``.plan(…)`` and ``.validate(…)``; ``entities.set``, ``entities.edit`` …
  ``project.*`` run on the server through a :class:`Connection`.
- :mod:`kentos.cad.types`: every input, output and plan type; exported here too.
- :data:`COMMANDS`: every wrapper by its command id; :func:`catalog`: the
  catalog itself, with its schemas and examples.

A refusal raises (:class:`CommandFailed` …) and writes nothing; a warning
goes to :mod:`warnings` (:class:`CommandWarning`). Coordinates are x east
(Y), y north (X), in metres in the project's plane whatever its drawing unit
(``Document.new(workspace="cad", drawing_unit="mm")``: a 4000 mm wall is
written 4.0; :class:`Units` converts; docs/adr/0245).
"""

